# CODEOWNERS
#
# GitHub uses the last matching pattern, so specific paths go after the wildcard.
# Owners are requested automatically on every pull request that touches a path.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS: every entry currently points at the repository owner because no
# specialist owners have been assigned yet. Replace them as roles are filled — do not
# guess a handle. A CODEOWNERS entry naming someone who does not exist silently stops
# requesting reviews, which is worse than no entry at all.
#
# Roles to assign (see docs/phase-4.5-backlog.md §"Suggested team allocation"):
#   contracts owner   — Solidity, scripts, deployment approval
#   database owner    — prisma schema, migrations, CI database jobs
#   security owner    — auth, guards, rate limiting, threat models
#   docs owner        — everything under docs/ and the root markdown files

# Default: everything not matched below.
